# Camelot Setlist — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env for local development, and/or enter the values under
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# None of them are required: the app runs with all of them missing, and each
# comment says what you lose without it.

# ——— Supabase (sign-in and storage) ———
# The two values from Supabase → Project → Settings → API.
# Both reach the browser and are not secret; Row Level Security protects the data.
# Without them: sign-in stays off and the app runs in guest mode (everything in the browser).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server side only: the catalog refresh writes with this, and session tokens are verified with it.
# SUPABASE_URL is the same address as above; the service_role key is on the Settings → API page.
# Never expose this to the browser (never give it a VITE_ prefix).
# Without them: the catalog cannot be written (`npm run seed:catalog` included) and web
# search cannot verify sessions.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ——— Other services ———

# Single-track lookup (GetSongBPM). Free key: https://getsongbpm.com/api
# Without it: the "search the web" button explains the key is missing instead of returning
# results; library and discovery-catalog search keep working.
GETSONGBPM_API_KEY=

# The weekly catalog refresh runs in GitHub Actions, not on Vercel; it needs the two
# SUPABASE_* values above as repository secrets. No extra variable is required here.
